---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SignalPost from '../components/SignalPost.astro';
import '../styles/observatory.css';
const notes = [
 ['01', 'Notice.', 'The workaround. The repeated frustration. The thing everyone has quietly accepted. That’s where we start.'],
 ['02', 'Understand.', 'We listen to the people living with it. We ask better questions before deciding what needs to be built.'],
 ['03', 'Make. Learn. Repeat.', 'Product and engineering turn an idea into something testable. Real use tells us what should happen next.']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Boomley — Good things begin with a better question.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <dialog class="opening" aria-label="Welcome to Boomley">
    <button class="opening-skip" type="button" autofocus>Skip intro ↗</button>
    <span class="micro">A SIGNAL FROM BOOMLEY</span>
    <p class="opening-line" aria-live="polite">The world keeps getting louder.</p>
    <div class="opening-end" hidden><span class="opening-brand">boomley<span>✳</span></span><p>Good things begin with a better question.</p><button class="action" type="button" data-enter>Explore what’s possible <span>↗</span></button></div>
    <span class="opening-thread" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </dialog>
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Boomley home">boomley<span aria-hidden="true">✳</span></a>
    <nav class="primary-nav" aria-label="Primary"><a href="#about">The idea</a><a href="#work">In the works <sup>01</sup></a><a href="#people">The people</a></nav>
    <a class="header-mail" href="#signal">Send a signal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-controls="mobile-menu" aria-expanded="false">Menu +</button>
    <nav class="mobile-menu" id="mobile-menu" aria-label="Mobile" hidden><a href="#about">The idea</a><a href="#work">In the works</a><a href="#people">The people</a><a href="#signal">Send a signal</a></nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <div class="hero-image" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/media/observatory/signal-lens-1536.webp" srcset="/media/observatory/signal-lens-640.webp 640w, /media/observatory/signal-lens-960.webp 960w, /media/observatory/signal-lens-1536.webp 1536w" sizes="100vw" width="1536" height="1024" alt="" fetchpriority="high"/></div>
      <div class="wrap hero-content"><div class="hero-overline micro"><span><i class="live-dot"></i> INDEPENDENT MINDS. SHARED CURIOSITY.</span><span class="edition">NOTICING THINGS / SINCE 2026</span></div><h1>What if<br/>things worked<br/><em>better?</em></h1><div class="hero-summary"><p>We’re Boomley. A two-person product company turning everyday problems into thoughtful digital products.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="action" href="#signal">Send us a signal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="quiet-link" href="#work">Meet our first build <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><span class="lens-note micro" aria-hidden="true">FIG. 01<br/>A LITTLE LESS NOISE.<br/>A LITTLE MORE ATTENTION.</span><div class="hero-bottom micro"><span>A PRODUCT COMPANY. AN OPEN WORKBENCH.</span><button class="motion-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Ⅱ Pause motion</button></div></div>
    </section>
    <div class="signal-strip" aria-hidden="true"><span>NOISE</span><pre data-ascii></pre><span class="signal-word">A SIGNAL ↗</span></div>
    <section id="about" class="section wrap about">
      <div class="section-top micro"><span>01 / A BETTER QUESTION</span><span>THE SMALL THINGS AREN’T ALWAYS SMALL.</span></div>
      <div class="manifesto"><h2 class="reveal">The workaround<br/>you stopped<br/><em>noticing?</em></h2><div class="manifesto-note reveal"><span class="note-pin" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="micro">FIELD NOTE / 001</span><p>“Why does it<br/>still have to<br/>be this hard?”</p><span class="micro">A PERFECTLY GOOD PLACE TO START.</span></div></div>
      <div class="about-bottom"><p class="about-answer">We haven’t.</p><div><p>Technology moves quickly. Everyday life doesn’t always get easier. We’re interested in that gap.</p><p>Boomley begins with the things people put up with: scattered attention, unnecessary steps, systems that ask too much. We investigate what matters—and build when something deserves to exist.</p><a class="quiet-link" href="#process">Here’s how we work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section id="work" class="work-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top micro"><span>02 / ON THE WORKBENCH</span><span>PRIVATE FOR NOW. PURPOSEFUL FROM THE START.</span></div><div class="work-layout"><div class="work-copy reveal"><span class="label"><i class="live-dot"></i> IN DEVELOPMENT</span><h2>Room for<br/><em>one thing.</em></h2><p>Our first investigation begins with fragmented attention—and what it takes to stay with something that matters.</p><p class="muted">We’re still working behind the scenes. Leave your email for a first look when 0001 is ready.</p><form class="waitlist" name="product-0001" method="POST" action="/thank-you" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field" data-waitlist><input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="product-0001"/><p class="honeypot"><label>Leave empty<input name="bot-field"/></label></p><label for="wait-email">Follow the first build</label><div class="email-row"><input id="wait-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="Your email address"/><button type="submit" aria-label="Join the 0001 update list">↗</button></div><p class="form-note">Only updates about 0001. Unsubscribe anytime.</p><p class="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></div><div class="specimen reveal" role="img" aria-label="A blue research folder labelled private product 0001"><div class="specimen-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div><span class="specimen-coord micro">BOOMLEY RESEARCH / OBJECT 0001</span><div class="folder"><div class="folder-back"></div><div class="folder-paper"><span class="micro">A QUESTION WE’RE WORKING ON</span><p>What if your tools<br/>made room for<br/><em>your attention?</em></p><div class="paper-lines"></div></div><div class="folder-front"><span class="micro">PRIVATE BUILD / DO NOT RUSH</span><strong>0001</strong><div class="folder-bottom micro"><span>PRODUCT + ENGINEERING</span><span>✳</span></div></div></div><span class="specimen-caption micro">SOME THINGS DESERVE A LITTLE MORE THOUGHT.</span></div></div></div></section>
    <section id="process" class="section wrap process"><div class="section-top micro"><span>03 / FROM FRICTION TO POSSIBILITY</span><span>OBSERVE. QUESTION. MAKE. REPEAT.</span></div><div class="process-intro"><h2>Curiosity,<br/><em>put to work.</em></h2><p>A good idea is a starting point.<br/>The people living with the problem<br/>help us find the way forward.</p></div><div class="process-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="observations"><span>the extra step</span><span>the workaround</span><span>the recurring problem</span></div><svg viewBox="0 0 800 180" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path class="process-track" d="M0 35C150 35 170 90 300 90H800M0 90H800M0 145C150 145 170 90 300 90"/><path class="process-line" d="M0 90H800"/></svg><div class="question-node">?</div><div class="test-node"><span>↗</span><small>A NEXT STEP</small></div></div><div class="process-notes">{notes.map(([n,title,body])=><article class="reveal"><span class="micro">{n}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="people" class="section wrap people"><div class="section-top micro"><span>04 / THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE QUESTIONS</span><span>TWO DISCIPLINES. ONE CONVERSATION.</span></div><div class="people-intro"><h2>Small team.<br/><em>Open minds.</em></h2><p>No layers of introductions.<br/>Just the two of us, figuring things out<br/>and making things happen.</p></div><div class="people-grid"><article class="person"><div class="portrait"><img src="/media/founders/chidi.webp" alt="Chidi, co-founder of Boomley" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"/><span class="portrait-tab micro">THE QUESTION / WHY?</span></div><div class="person-name"><h3>Chidi</h3><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><span class="micro">PRODUCT & STRATEGY</span><p>Research, product thinking, and the experience of the person using it.</p></article><article class="person person-michael"><div class="portrait"><img src="/media/founders/michael.webp" alt="Michael, co-founder of Boomley" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"/><span class="portrait-tab micro">THE QUESTION / HOW?</span></div><div class="person-name"><h3>Michael</h3><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><span class="micro">SOFTWARE ENGINEERING</span><p>Systems, architecture, and turning a good question into something real.</p></article></div></section>
    <section id="community" class="community"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top micro"><span>05 / AN OPEN INVITATION</span><span>FOR THE QUIETLY CURIOUS.</span></div><div class="community-layout"><h2>There’s room<br/>for your<br/><em>“what if?”</em></h2><div><span class="community-mark" aria-hidden="true">[ ✳ ]</span><p>The problem-noticers. The developers. The designers, researchers, students, and people who see things a little differently.</p><p>Bring a question, an idea, or a way you’d like to help. You don’t have to be a builder to belong.</p><a class="quiet-link" href="mailto:hello@boomley.com?subject=Building%20with%20Boomley">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
    <SignalPost/>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer wrap"><div class="footer-top"><p>Something on your mind?<br/><em>That’s how it starts.</em></p><a href="mailto:hello@boomley.com">hello@boomley.com ↗</a></div><a class="footer-brand" href="#top" aria-label="Boomley, back to top">boomley<span>✳</span></a><div class="footer-bottom micro"><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} BOOMLEY</span><a href="/privacy">Privacy & your signal</a><a href="#top">BACK TO THE TOP ↑</a></div></footer>
  <script>import '../scripts/observatory.ts';</script>
</BaseLayout>
